      5 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تليّث</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَيَّثَ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُيِّثَ</span> <i>He</i> (a man, TA,)
<i>became like the Benoo-Leyth,</i> or, <i>like a lion, in
desire;</i> expl. by <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَارَ لَيْثِىَّ الهَوَى</span>; (K;) <i>and in
zeal in the cause of his party:</i> (TA:) <i>he became
like a lion;</i> as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِسْتَلْيَثَ</span></b> . (L.)

